% A second -v adds a note for the first comparison in each rule that ordered
% values of different types, which is false: one for small and one for
% between, whose second comparison is never reached by a mixed binding, and
% none for same, whose = is defined across types.  The note names the types
% of the values compared, which for quoted, whose = admits only the string,
% are a string and an integer.  Answers are unchanged.
v(1).
v(a).
v(b).
v("s").
small(X) :- v(X), X < 5.
between(X) :- v(X), X > 0,
    X < 9.
same(X) :- v(X), X = a.
quoted(X) :- v(X), X = "s", X < 5.

small(X)?
between(X)?
same(X)?
quoted(X)?
